    "q-76948": {
      "dom_id": "step-q76948",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "$24\\text{ mod }8=$",
      "worked_solution": "The residue of $24$ modulo $8$ is the integer $0\\le r<8$ such that\n\n$$\n24≡r\\,(\\text{mod}\\,8).\n$$\n\n**Method 1**\n\nTo find the residue $r,$ we need to write $24$ as an integer multiple of $8,$ plus the residue $r.$\n\nWe note that $24≡0\\,(\\text{mod}\\,8)$ because\n\n$$\n24=3\\cdot 8+0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the residue of $24$ modulo $8$ is $0.$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nWe can use the subtraction property:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}24 & ≡24-0 &  & (\\text{mod}\\,8) \\\\  & ≡24-3\\cdot 8 &  & (\\text{mod}\\,8) \\\\  & ≡24-24 &  & (\\text{mod}\\,8) \\\\  & ≡0 &  & (\\text{mod}\\,8)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the residue of $24$ modulo $8$ is $0.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
