    "q-213026": {
      "dom_id": "step-q213026",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "$21\\text{ mod }5=${{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "The residue of $21$ modulo $5$ is the integer $0\\le r<5$ such that\n\n$$\n21≡r\\,(\\text{mod}\\,5).\n$$\n\n**Method 1**\n\nTo find the residue $r,$ we need to write $21$ as an integer multiple of $5,$ plus the residue $r.$\n\nWe note that $21≡1\\,(\\text{mod}\\,5)$ because\n\n$$\n21=4\\cdot 5+1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the residue of $21$ modulo $5$ is $1.$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nWe can use the subtraction property:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}21 & ≡21-0 &  & (\\text{mod}\\,5) \\\\  & ≡21-4\\cdot 5 &  & (\\text{mod}\\,5) \\\\  & ≡21-20 &  & (\\text{mod}\\,5) \\\\  & ≡1 &  & (\\text{mod}\\,5)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the residue of $21$ modulo $5$ is $1.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
