    "q-213028": {
      "dom_id": "step-q213028",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "$64\\text{ mod }5=${{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "The residue of $64$ modulo $5$ is the integer $0\\le r<5$ such that\n\n$$\n64≡r\\,(\\text{mod}\\,5).\n$$\n\n**Method 1**\n\nTo find the residue $r,$ we need to write $64$ as an integer multiple of $5,$ plus the residue $r.$\n\nWe note that $64≡4\\,(\\text{mod}\\,5)$ because\n\n$$\n64=12\\cdot 5+4.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the residue of $64$ modulo $5$ is $4.$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nWe can use the subtraction property:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}64 & ≡64-0 &  & (\\text{mod}\\,5) \\\\  & ≡64-12\\cdot 5 &  & (\\text{mod}\\,5) \\\\  & ≡64-60 &  & (\\text{mod}\\,5) \\\\  & ≡4 &  & (\\text{mod}\\,5)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the residue of $64$ modulo $5$ is $4.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
