    "q-102403": {
      "dom_id": "step-q102403",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "$61\\text{ mod }7=$",
      "worked_solution": "The residue of $61$ modulo $7$ is the integer $0\\le r<7$ such that\n\n$$\n61≡r\\,(\\text{mod}\\,7).\n$$\n\n**Method 1**\n\nTo find the residue $r,$ we need to write $61$ as an integer multiple of $7,$ plus the residue $r.$\n\nWe note that $61≡5\\,(\\text{mod}\\,7)$ because\n\n$$\n61=8\\cdot 7+5.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the residue of $61$ modulo $7$ is $5.$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nWe can use the subtraction property:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}61 & ≡61-0 &  & (\\text{mod}\\,7) \\\\  & ≡61-8\\cdot 7 &  & (\\text{mod}\\,7) \\\\  & ≡61-56 &  & (\\text{mod}\\,7) \\\\  & ≡5 &  & (\\text{mod}\\,7)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the residue of $61$ modulo $7$ is $5.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
