    "q-102409": {
      "dom_id": "step-q102409",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "$-37\\text{ mod }5=$",
      "worked_solution": "The residue of $-37$ modulo $5$ is the integer $0\\le r<5$ such that\n\n$$\n-37≡r\\,(\\text{mod}\\,5).\n$$\n\n**Method 1**\n\nTo find the residue $r,$ we need to write $-37$ as an integer multiple of $5,$ plus the residue $r.$\n\nWe note that $-37≡3\\,(\\text{mod}\\,5)$ because\n\n$$\n-37=(-8)\\cdot 5+3.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the residue of $-37$ modulo $5$ is $3.$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nWe can use the addition property:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-37 & ≡-37+0 &  & (\\text{mod}\\,5) \\\\  & ≡-37+8\\cdot 5 &  & (\\text{mod}\\,5) \\\\  & ≡-37+40 &  & (\\text{mod}\\,5) \\\\  & ≡3 &  & (\\text{mod}\\,5)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the residue of $-37$ modulo $5$ is $3.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
