    "q-213076": {
      "dom_id": "step-q213076",
      "name": "Question 8",
      "problem": "$-7\\text{ mod }2=${{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "The residue of $-7$ modulo $2$ is the integer $0\\le r<2$ such that\n\n$$\n-7≡r\\,(\\text{mod}\\,2).\n$$\n\n**Method 1**\n\nTo find the residue $r,$ we need to write $-7$ as an integer multiple of $2,$ plus the residue $r.$\n\nWe note that $-7≡1\\,(\\text{mod}\\,2)$ because\n\n$$\n-7=(-4)\\cdot 2+1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the residue of $-7$ modulo $2$ is $1.$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nWe can use the addition property:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-7 & ≡-7+0 &  & (\\text{mod}\\,2) \\\\  & ≡-7+4\\cdot 2 &  & (\\text{mod}\\,2) \\\\  & ≡-7+8 &  & (\\text{mod}\\,2) \\\\  & ≡1 &  & (\\text{mod}\\,2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the residue of $-7$ modulo $2$ is $1.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
