    "q-76965": {
      "dom_id": "step-q76965",
      "name": "Question 9",
      "problem": "$-27\\text{ mod }8=$",
      "worked_solution": "The residue of $-27$ modulo $8$ is the integer $0\\le r<8$ such that\n\n$$\n-27≡r\\,(\\text{mod}\\,8).\n$$\n\n**Method 1**\n\nTo find the residue $r,$ we need to write $-27$ as an integer multiple of $8,$ plus the residue $r.$\n\nWe note that $-27≡5\\,(\\text{mod}\\,8)$ because\n\n$$\n-27=(-4)\\cdot 8+5.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the residue of $-27$ modulo $8$ is $5.$  \n\n**Method 2**\n\nWe can use the addition property:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-27 & ≡-27+0 &  & (\\text{mod}\\,8) \\\\  & ≡-27+4\\cdot 8 &  & (\\text{mod}\\,8) \\\\  & ≡-27+32 &  & (\\text{mod}\\,8) \\\\  & ≡5 &  & (\\text{mod}\\,8)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the residue of $-27$ modulo $8$ is $5.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
