    "q-213083": {
      "dom_id": "step-q213083",
      "name": "Question 10",
      "problem": "$-61\\text{ mod }5=${{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "The residue of $-61$ modulo $5$ is the integer $0\\le r<5$ such that\n\n$$\n-61≡r\\,(\\text{mod}\\,5).\n$$\n\n**Method 1**\n\nTo find the residue $r,$ we need to write $-61$ as an integer multiple of $5,$ plus the residue $r.$\n\nWe note that $-61≡4\\,(\\text{mod}\\,5)$ because\n\n$$\n-61=(-13)\\cdot 5+4.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the residue of $-61$ modulo $5$ is $4.$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nWe can use the addition property:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-61 & ≡-61+0 &  & (\\text{mod}\\,5) \\\\  & ≡-61+13\\cdot 5 &  & (\\text{mod}\\,5) \\\\  & ≡-61+65 &  & (\\text{mod}\\,5) \\\\  & ≡4 &  & (\\text{mod}\\,5)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the residue of $-61$ modulo $5$ is $4.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
